Spec: Semester entity and semester view

Purpose:
  The Semester entity (year and term) and a multi-column vertical list calendar (wall planner) showing one semester
  on one desktop screen. Each month is a column and each day is a row. The view is a read-only aggregation over
  ../courses/courses.sdd, ../realizations/realizations.sdd, ../lessons/lessons.sdd and ../holidays/holidays.sdd.

Owns:
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py
  ./view.py
  ./routes.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../courses/courses.sdd
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd
  ../lessons/lessons.sdd
  ../holidays/holidays.sdd
  ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd

Must:
  A Semester has a year and a term of `spring` or `fall`; the year and term combination is unique.
  @SemesterRepository in ./ports.py exposes list, get and add operations backing ./services.py.
  The semester periods are the four periods of academic year `2026-2027`, with semesters spanning the period groups
  `2026-08-01` to `2026-12-31` and `2027-01-01` to `2027-07-31`.
  The container is a CSS grid whose `grid-template-columns` is `repeat(`, one column per month of the selected
  semester, `, 1fr)`, and `gap: 10px`. A semester of five months renders five columns.
  The container height is `100vh` minus the header height, so a 1080p screen shows the whole semester without
  vertical or horizontal scrolling.
  The view is desktop-only and has no mobile responsiveness.
  Each month is a flex column (`display: flex; flex-direction: column`) with the month name as header at its top.
  Each month contains one row per day of that month, and each row has `flex: 1` so all rows share height equally.
  A day row shows the weekday abbreviation, the date number and a wider space for lesson indicators.
  Lessons appear as inline-block squares of `12px` by `12px`. The view assigns each CourseRealization a color from a
  fixed palette at render time; no color is stored in the database.
  Hovering a square shows lesson details through a pure CSS tooltip that does not change the row height.
  Holidays are visibly distinguished on their day row and show their title.
  For the admin, clicking a day row opens the dialog specified in ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd.

Example:
  semester 1: `2026-08` to `2026-12`
  columns: `repeat(5, 1fr)`
  semester 2: `2027-01` to `2027-07`
  columns: `repeat(7, 1fr)`

Tasks:
  [?] Decide whether arbitrary Semesters are creatable by the admin or only the current hardcoded `2026-2027`
    academic year is supported for now
  [ ] Implement @Semester, @SemesterRepository and the SQLite adapter
  [ ] Render the static month columns and day rows
  [ ] Render lesson squares and CSS tooltips through ../realizations/realizations.sdd, ../lessons/lessons.sdd and
    ../courses/courses.sdd services
  [ ] Render holidays through ../holidays/holidays.sdd services
